# jpadsite lane — evidence manifest
# Identify by content, not by path: these files live at two host paths
# (_jpadsite_priv/evidence and AI_IC_design/jpadsite_evidence/evidence),
# and both are coordinates the world is free to move. The sha256 is not.
#
# THIS FILE IS NOT IN `sha256sum -c` FORMAT, despite the .sha256 name.
# `sha256sum -c MANIFEST.sha256` reads ZERO lines from it. MEASURED: it exits 1
# and prints nothing at all to stdout, saying why only on stderr. So it does not
# hand you a false green — it hands you SILENCE, which is worse in a pipeline
# that greps stdout for ': FAILED' and finds none. Verify with the parser instead:
#     python3 verify_manifest.py          # rc 0 pass / 1 fail / 2 undetermined
# It also fails on any file present on disk and absent here, so the manifest
# cannot go quietly stale by addition.
#
# verify_manifest.py, and after adding English renderings beside the six quoted
# L-document lines in RESULT.md. Branch jpadsite/pad-site @ 725f9352f (FROZEN);
# NOTE: editing any file below invalidates this manifest — regenerate it
#       in the same breath, or the fingerprints describe a prior state.
# REGENERATED 2026-08-22 after adding english_only_check.py,
# verify_manifest.py and the generated OMITTED_BY_GITIGNORE.md.
# Ten .log/.def entries below are dropped by .gitignore on the published
# branch; verify_manifest.py reads the omission declaration and reports
# each by name as ABSENT-BY-DESIGN. Branch jpadsite/pad-site @ 725f9352f
# (FROZEN); main ae78abb28.
